---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout>
	<div class="content">
        <div class="page-section">
            <h1>About</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="page-section">
            <h2>Who We Are</h2>
            <p>
                We're a small family run coffee roasting business based out of Doylestown Pennsylvania
            </p>
            <p>
                We specialize in roasting small batches of single origin coffees to perfectly bring out the unique
                flavors of each individual coffee variety.
            </p>
            <p>
                We believe on local and fresh. The sooner the coffee gets to you and the fewer miles it has to travel
                the more flavor it has and the less the impact to the environment.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="page-section">
            <h2>What Makes Great Coffee</h2>
            <h3>Quality Green Beans</h3>
            <p>
                We roast quality single origin green coffee sourced from our favorite cofee growing regions around the world.
            </p>
            <p>
                We believe single origin coffee is the best way to experience and explore the unique tastes of each variety.
            </p>
            <h3>The Roast</h3>
            <p>
                There is a lot to get right to truly roast coffee well and just throwing coffee in a roaster for a while and 
                hoping for the best isn't going to cut it. By roasting with equipment which gives us detailed data on what's 
                happening in the roast, we roast each batch perfectly.
            </p>
            <h3>Fresh Beans</h3>
            <p>
                Roasted coffee is best between 3-5 days and 2 weeks after roasting. If it's not 'rested'
                for a few days after roasting, you might not get the full flavor of the coffee. If it's
                too old, the best flavors will have started to fade and the coffee will start to taste
                flat and empty.
            </p>
            <h3>Grind Immediately Before Use</h3>
            <p>
                The whole coffee bean acts as a little sealed container keeping in the best flavors and aromas. Grind your coffee
                immediately before you brew it to keep the best of those flavors in the coffee all the way to the cup.
            </p>
            <h3>Brew It Well</h3>
            <p>There are lots of great ways to brew coffee. We prefer Espresso with water to make Americano,
                or a V60 pourover. We usually find that traditional home drip machines don't make the best
                coffee, so if you're not getting the most out of your cup, consider buying a cheap v60 dripper
                and experimenting!
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</PageLayout>
